## 2. Environments & Responsiveness (critical — must be handled explicitly)

The app runs on desktop browsers, Android phones, and iPhones. Handle all of the following:

- **Breakpoints (Tailwind):** mobile `< 640px`, tablet `640–1024px`, desktop `> 1024px`. Every screen must be tested and correct at all three widths.
- **Touch-first:** all interactive targets ≥ 44×44px. No hover-only interactions — every hover action must also work on tap. Provide `:active`/pressed states for touch feedback.
- **Custom cursor** (the cyan dot + trailing ring from the reference design) is **desktop-with-mouse only** — disable it entirely on touch devices (detect via `(pointer: coarse)`), and fall back to the native cursor.
- **`prefers-reduced-motion`:** when set, disable the particle animation, floating/rotating hero motion, and large transitions; keep the UI fully usable and static.
- **Mobile navigation:** a fixed bottom navigation bar on mobile (الرئيسية / الأقسام / السلة / حسابي) with safe-area insets (`env(safe-area-inset-bottom)`) so it clears the iPhone home indicator. Desktop uses the top navbar instead.
- **iOS specifics:** respect safe-area insets top/bottom; ensure `100dvh` (not `100vh`) is used for full-height sections so mobile browser chrome doesn't clip content; ensure the install/add-to-home-screen path works in Safari.
- **Performance on mobile:** reduce particle count on small screens (e.g. ~40 particles on mobile vs ~110 on desktop) and lazy-mount heavy visual effects.

