## 5. Auth Routing (simulated in this frontend task)

- A single login form at `/login` (Arabic). On submit, simulate authentication against mock users.
- Mock users include at least: one `Customer` and one `SuperAdmin`.
- After login: if the signed-in role is `Admin` or `SuperAdmin` → redirect to `/admin`. Otherwise → redirect to the storefront home `/`.
- `AuthContext` holds the current mock user + role. Admin routes are guarded: if role is not Admin/SuperAdmin, redirect to `/login`. (This is UI-level guarding for now; real server enforcement comes with the backend later.)
- Provide a visible way to switch/log out for testing.

